<title>ITALY: Costa Crociere '96 pretax profit rises.</title>
<headline>Costa Crociere '96 pretax profit rises.</headline>
<dateline>GENOA, Italy 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ending December 31, 1996 (in billion lire unless stated):</p>
<p>    Cons net profit		    88.5     vs   48.4</p>
<p>    Parent net profit		 110.2     vs   20.2</p>
<p>    Cons turnover		   1,105.7     vs  965</p>
<p>    Cons operating result	    55.1     vs   35.7</p>
<p>    Parent sales			958.4     vs  895.5</p>
<p>Note - Italian cruise line Costa Crociere Spa said it decided to leave decisions on ordinary share dividends to a shaerholders' meeting in light of a public offer to buy (OPA) which starts on May 16.</p>
<p>It envisaged paying 75 lire per savings share for 1996 after a savings share dividend of 140 lire in 1995 and 120 lire ofr ordinary shares.</p>
<p>--Milan bureau +392 66129507</p>
